  "body": "Adds 400 numbered informal entries in algebra, finite geometry, combinatorics and analysis: 379 proved lemmas/theorems and 21 explicitly unproved conjectures or research proposals. Each proved entry includes its hypotheses, English proof and use; each research target separates evidence from proof and records its literature-status limits.\n\nThe atlas builds on inspected declarations in the canonical Lean tree, bounded read-only DAG retrieval and primary literature. It includes proofs of prime-phase codimension-one flat completion and deficiency-one symplectic spread completion, explicit symplectic chart transitions, weighted minimum-noise reconstruction, finite moment recovery and rectangular closest-isometry repair. These are mathematical derivations and classical reconstructions, without a global novelty claim.\n\nValidation: all 400 statements and proof/evidence blocks received author and separate-agent review; final source hashes, the entry catalogue, local links and packaged SHA-256 manifest pass the included validator. Exact duplicate topics were replaced or given a distinct additional conclusion. The collection is informal and claims no new Lean formalization, kernel verification, multiplication-exponent improvement, or solution of its conjectures. Historical source and PR credits are retained in the attribution records.",
